1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,836
Welcome to our School Leadership
Professional Learning Workshop.

2
00:00:07,836 --> 00:00:11,609
Today we're going to explore Autistic
experience and what it

3
00:00:11,609 --> 00:00:14,629
means for access, belonging and
partnership across a school.

4
00:00:14,629 --> 00:00:17,770
Keep the students you work with at the
centre of the day.

5
00:00:17,770 --> 00:00:21,911
We'll build our understanding, look
closely at everyday school

6
00:00:21,911 --> 00:00:25,094
routines and consider what we can change
in the environment, the

7
00:00:25,094 --> 00:00:26,909
task and the support we offer.

8
00:00:26,909 --> 00:00:30,765
Our starting point is curiosity. We are
here to understand

9
00:00:30,765 --> 00:00:33,192
students and make participation more
workable.

10
00:00:33,396 --> 00:00:37,129
We value students as they are and support
their participation

11
00:00:37,129 --> 00:00:38,007
and belonging.

12
00:00:38,007 --> 00:00:41,781
You don't need to arrive with all the
answers. Bring your

13
00:00:41,781 --> 00:00:44,555
questions, your experience and a
willingness to look again.

14
00:00:44,555 --> 00:00:48,329
As leaders you shape the conditions in
which that understanding

15
00:00:48,329 --> 00:00:50,022
becomes everyday practice.

16
00:00:50,022 --> 00:00:53,755
We will keep different students in view as
we look at school

17
00:00:53,755 --> 00:00:56,489
routines, culture, resourcing and
partnership.

18
00:00:58,681 --> 00:01:03,603
I acknowledge the Traditional Custodians
of the lands on which we are learning

19
00:01:03,604 --> 00:01:08,718
today, and pay my respects to Elders past
and present. I recognise the continuing

20
00:01:08,719 --> 00:01:13,258
connections of Aboriginal and Torres
Strait Islander peoples to Country,

21
00:01:13,259 --> 00:01:18,053
culture and community. I extend that
respect to Aboriginal and Torres Strait

22
00:01:18,054 --> 00:01:21,249
Islander people taking part in this
